# Diagnose first, then wait

When something is broken, missing, or blocked:

1. Say what failed, in plain language.
2. Say the likely cause.
3. Stop. Do not implement a workaround, rewrite a cell, or change the approach yet.

Only build an alternative after the user clearly asks — for example "make the solution", "do the workaround", or "go ahead".

```text
❌ BAD
Clone failed, so I will zip the repo and rewrite the notebook.

✅ GOOD
Clone failed because the GitHub repo is private, so Colab cannot log in.
Say if you want a workaround.
```

Do not treat "what is wrong?" or "do I need to change anything?" as permission to implement. Answer the question. Wait for the go-ahead.
